Actually, the potions spoiler says each potion restores one lost level
up to a maximum of *half* the levels lost, and the source and my own
wizard testing bears this out, more or less.  More exactly, each
potion quaffed when your current level is below your maximum will
decrease the maximum level and increase your own level (but if they
cross, the maximum will be set to the increased current), like so:

                /* Restore one lost level if blessed */
                if (otmp->blessed && u.ulevel < u.ulevelmax) {
                    /* when multiple levels have been lost, drinking
                       multiple potions will only get half of them
                back */
                    u.ulevelmax -= 1;
                    pluslvl(FALSE);
                }

You can lose two levels safely, but if you lose three levels from 30
to 27, you get back to 28 for killing the vampire, but the first
b!PofFH bumps your current level up to 29 and your max level down to
29, and the next b!PofFH won't do anything.

Perhaps you only tested two levels, or maybe you accidentally wished
for potions of gain level instead of full healing?

